'' vendor/libpq -- libpq, PostgreSQL's C client library (PostgreSQL 19.0), with TLS through
'' OpenSSL 3.5, as one import:
''
''     #import "vendor/libpq" link dynamic        (or 'link static', or neither)
''
'' Every routine, type and constant of libpq-fe.h (and postgres_ext.h, which it includes) is
'' then callable as PostgreSQL documents it, unqualified -- PQconnectdb, PQexecParams,
'' CONNECTION_OK, PGRES_TUPLES_OK.
''
'' THE HEADERS are libpq-fe.ti and postgres_ext.ti, translated by 'tiko c2t' and committed; their
'' banners name the C headers and their SHA-256. libpq-residue.ti holds by hand what the
'' translation could not carry: OID_MAX, atooid, PQsetdb.
''
'' A query with a parameter -- never splice values into SQL text:
''
''     dim as PGconn ptr c = PQconnectdb( "host=db.example.com dbname=app user=app sslmode=verify-full" )
''     if PQstatus( c ) <> CONNECTION_OK then print *PQerrorMessage( c ) : end 1
''     dim as const zstring ptr vals( 0 to 0 ) = { strptr( "42" ) }
''     dim as PGresult ptr r = PQexecParams( c, "select name from item where id = $1", 1, _
''                                           nullptr, @vals( 0 ), nullptr, nullptr, 0 )
''     if PQresultStatus( r ) = PGRES_TUPLES_OK andalso PQntuples( r ) > 0 then print *PQgetvalue( r, 0, 0 )
''     PQclear( r ) : PQfinish( c )
''
'' What libpq allocates, libpq frees: PQclear for a PGresult, PQfinish for a connection (also one
'' that failed), PQfreemem for PQnotifies' records, PQescapeLiteral's and PQunescapeBytea's
'' results. A value from PQgetvalue lives as long as its PGresult.
''
'' TLS: OpenSSL is inside the library -- nothing else to ship. 'sslmode=verify-full' checks the
'' server's certificate chain and its name; give the roots with 'sslrootcert=<file>', or
'' 'sslrootcert=system' for the operating system's. libpq's default, 'prefer', encrypts when the
'' server offers it and verifies nothing.
''
'' THE LIBRARY: with 'link static' libpq and OpenSSL are linked into the program; with 'link
'' dynamic' -- and when no '#import' says, which is this package's default -- the shared library,
'' which tiko copies beside the program: libpq.dll on Windows, libpq_linux_x86_64.so or
'' libpq_linux_arm64.so on Linux, libpq_macos_arm64.dylib on macOS.
#module "libpq"

public #include once "postgres_ext.ti"
public #include once "libpq-fe.ti"
public #include once "libpq-residue.ti"

#ifdef TIKO_LINK_STATIC
    '' A static libpq on Windows needs what its OpenSSL and libpq.dll would have imported.
    #ifdef TIKO_OS_WINDOWS
        #foreignlib PQ static "lib/libpq", "system:ws2_32", "system:secur32", "system:crypt32", _
                              "system:advapi32", "system:user32", "system:shell32"
    #else
        #foreignlib PQ static "lib/libpq", "system:m"
    #endif
#else
    #foreignlib PQ dynamic "lib/libpq"
#endif
